1
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,340
Be careful. Load it up.

2
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,240
Load it up.

3
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:11,400
Don't rush.

4
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,240
Slow down.

5
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:33,250
Who's there?

6
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,039
Stop!

7
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,120
Stop!

8
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,280
Stop!

9
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,800
Turn off the flashlight, quick!

10
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,120
Take two men

11
00:01:53,759 --> 00:01:54,720
and flank them from behind.

12
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:55,880
Okay, understood.

13
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:21,760
Guang.

14
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:23,480
Man,

15
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,920
these guys move too fast.

16
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,280
They know the woods well.

17
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,800
I reckon

18
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,200
they're not ordinary timber thieves.

19
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,000
Nonsense.

20
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:34,920
Four people

21
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:37,170
ran away right under our noses.

22
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,280
You guys stay alert.

23
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,440
The road is too slippery.

24
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:44,040
Is the job done?

25
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,400
No.

26
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:47,810
This is the last batch of goods.

27
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,880
Can you guys give me a break?

28
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:53,440
Move!

29
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:56,640
Catch him!

30
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,720
Hands on your head!

31
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,600
Don't move. Cuff him.

32
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:01,240
Hands on your head. Get down.

33
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:03,760
Officer,

34
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,940
this is our first time doing this.

35
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,440
We won't dare do it again.

36
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,600
First time?

37
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,480
Looking at your setup,

38
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,480
you treat the reserve's

39
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,210
core forest area like your own garden, don't you?

40
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,400
Handcuff them.

41
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:17,260
Take them all back to the station.

42
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:18,650
Get up. Let's go.

43
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:19,600
Look.

44
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,060
Behave.

45
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:20,770
Hurry up.

46
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,000
No.

47
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:25,040
Let's talk it over.

48
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,200
What good wood.

49
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,280
Take it to the Forest Protection Section.

50
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:29,880
Okay.

51
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,280
Forest Protection Section.

52
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,680
We caught a truckload at the mountain pass.

53
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,480
Boss Hu.

54
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,800
It seems we've been exposed.

55
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,490
Let's hurry up and retreat.

56
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,340
Tell Xiaohu's side

57
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,480
to speed up.

58
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,480
Man,

59
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,560
it's Uncle Hu.

60
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,440
Is Xiaohu still with you?

61
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:56,920
He already left.

62
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,280
Left?

63
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,000
Where did he go?

64
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,440
I don't know.

65
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,490
If he contacts you or goes to see you again,

66
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:07,560
keep him there

67
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,920
and give me a call.

68
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,840
I'm begging you.

69
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,560
He is my only son.

70
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,760
As for Xiaohu,

71
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:18,440
please help him if you can.

72
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,120
Okay?

73
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,480
Xiaoman.

74
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:30,690
Come with me.

75
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:32,520
Come here.

76
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,330
Xiaoman.

77
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:47,000
I went to the empty room in the backyard during the day

78
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,060
and saw that someone had lived there.

79
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:51,780
It was Teng Xiaohu, wasn't it?

80
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,360
And

81
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,080
the things in my drawer

82
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,240
were also taken by Teng Xiaohu,

83
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,040
weren't they?

84
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:58,320
I...

85
00:04:58,440 --> 00:04:58,880
You...

86
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,920
How could you be so silly?

87
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:04,920
How many times have I told you

88
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:08,410
that no one is allowed to touch the things in that drawer?

89
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,600
Do you know what he took?

90
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,240
Mr. Song.

91
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,600
I don't know.

92
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,360
He eavesdropped on our conversation that day

93
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:16,560
and picked your lock.

94
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,200
I don't know what he took.

95
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,520
Do you know

96
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,360
he will get us killed?

97
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,120
They are capable of anything.

98
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,320
I almost lost my life back then.

99
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:29,880
Xiaoman,

100
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,280
this is my last warning to you today.

101
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:34,010
I've already locked that door.

102
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:34,920
If

103
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,920
you keep seeing Teng Xiaohu,

104
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,540
you can stop working here.

105
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,680
Mr. Song.

106
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:40,960
I won't.

107
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:42,770
I won't do it again. I was wrong.

108
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:45,960
Xiaoman.

109
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:47,840
Look how old I am.

110
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,600
How many years do I have left?

111
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:52,440
Why do I keep stopping you time and time again?

112
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,280
I treat you like my own daughter,

113
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,120
you know?

114
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,040
Mr. Song.

115
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,360
He's gone.

116
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:59,330
He'll never come back. Really.

117
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:01,680
Forget it.

118
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,440
It's been 16 years.

119
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:08,780
What's meant to come has come.

120
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,880
Maybe this is God's will.

121
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:13,920
Xiaoman.

122
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,920
What I'm about to say,

123
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,320
you must remember it well.

124
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,120
If one day in the future,

125
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:23,920
I...

126
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,320
If one day,

127
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:31,240
someone comes to you

128
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,840
and asks about what happened 16 years ago,

129
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,400
you know nothing.

130
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:40,780
Do you remember what I told you last time?

131
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,040
You're saying

132
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,700
Wang Hong is that kid from the Zhao family back then?

133
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:50,400
Stop eating.

134
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,120
How can you be so carefree?

135
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,960
If we alert them,

136
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,880
it'll be hard to find them again.

137
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,400
Uncle,

138
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:58,440
let me eat my fill before we look for them.

139
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,960
Isn't it the same if we look after eating?

140
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:01,160
Eat, eat, eat.

141
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:13,600
Can you stop smacking your lips when eating instant noodles?

142
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,360
Boss,

143
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:16,450
add another sausage for me.

144
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:18,600
Don't rush.

145
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,400
I remember now.

146
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,800
In the woods just now,

147
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:25,260
I saw that guy with the afro running in front.

148
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,480
The day we first met Uncle Wang,

149
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,280
he was

150
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,440
smacking his lips while eating there.

151
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,000
Did you see clearly what he looked like?

152
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,280
No need to see his face.

153
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,240
That afro,

154
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:35,000
it's

155
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,320
so obvious.

156
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,080
Go to the internet cafe.

157
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:38,920
Have you seen

158
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,200
this person?

159
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:43,780
Never seen him.

160
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,440
Take a closer look.

161
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,240
I don't recall.

162
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,320
Officer,

163
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,360
I'm a person

164
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,400
who never lies.

165
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:53,880
Be honest.

166
00:07:54,159 --> 00:07:55,600
Just answer what you're asked.

167
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,159
Okay.

168
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,360
I promise

169
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,320
to tell you

170
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:58,980
everything

171
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,160
I know.

172
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:03,160
The batch of wood you transported tonight,

173
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:04,280
where is its destination?

174
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:05,960
Just the Beishan intersection.

175
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,090
A car will pick it up.

176
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,400
We just earn money for our hard work.

177
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,450
I really don't know anything else.

178
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:16,450
You question him first.

179
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:17,720
Wait,

180
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:19,760
officer.

181
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:21,960
Can I see that photo again?

182
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:23,860
You recognize him?

183
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,480
I think

184
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,410
he looks a bit familiar.

185
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:33,919
Look closely.

186
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,240
I think I've seen him somewhere.

187
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,559
But he has hair.

188
00:08:42,559 --> 00:08:43,760
He has hair.

189
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:55,320
What time is it? Will he still come?

190
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,800
Wait a little longer.

191
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,170
Careful, don't burn yourself.

192
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:18,880
Here.

193
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,060
Come on, follow me this round.

194
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:22,880
Let's go.

195
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:35,160
Continue.

196
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:36,220
You guys continue.

197
00:09:59,040 --> 00:09:59,920
That's him.

198
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,160
He's out.

199
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:08,640
That's him.

200
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,120
It's really vivid.

201
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:34,520
Brother,

202
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,930
there's activity on the forum.

203
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,240
The year and quantity

204
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:40,170
match the batch we're looking for.

205
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:52,320
Xin F 66573

206
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,200
Thank you.

207
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:55,960
What's the matter? Why the rush?

208
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,120
I was playing a game.

209
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,170
Look at the work you did at home.

210
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:01,250
How did you sort those logs?

211
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:06,490
I... I'll fix it.

212
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:09,650
I was just saying my eyelids

213
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:12,100
have been twitching these past two days.

214
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,640
Ergui.

215
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:58,890
Let's go.

216
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,250
It's this batch of wood.

217
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,650
These are the ones I marked.

218
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,300
I've been looking for them for so many years.

219
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,200
They were hidden here.

220
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,720
We found them.

221
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,440
That's a good thing.

222
00:13:45,440 --> 00:13:47,480
Teng Laohu must have done this.

223
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,500
It might not have been Teng Laohu.

224
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:53,090
But it definitely went through his hands.

225
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,760
The ledger was found in his office.

226
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:58,690
He's definitely involved in this.

227
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,680
Uncle Wang.

228
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,840
This batch of wood is very important to you, right?

229
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:11,080
It's almost dawn.

230
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:13,020
Should we leave first?

231
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:15,900
How about this.

232
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,850
Let's go to the entrance

233
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:19,120
and wait for him a bit.

234
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,040
Let's go.
